# Sphere backend (sphere-quest) — marketplace, user installed-apps, auth
VITE_SPHERE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Developer Portal — "Open developer portal" / "Submit your project" CTAs link here
VITE_DEV_PORTAL_URL=https://developers.staging.unicity.network/

# Aggregator (state-transition gateway) API key.
# The testnet2 value below is NOT a secret — safe to keep here and in docs.
# For mainnet this MUST be a real secret: set it only in the deploy env, never commit it.
# Used ONLY when subscriptions are OFF: with VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_ENABLED=true the
# per-wallet SGW key replaces it and this value is ignored entirely.
VITE_AGGREGATOR_API_KEY=sk_ddc3cfcc001e4a28ac3fad7407f99590

# wallet-api backend (S4 provider swap). When set, the ASSET path rides the
# wallet-api backend (server inventory custody + mailbox delivery + §16
# payment requests); messaging/DMs/nametags stay on Nostr. Unset → the legacy
# local-custody composition. Relative values resolve against the app origin
# and are served by the dev/preview proxy, which forwards them to
# WALLET_API_PROXY_TARGET (default http://127.0.0.1:3000 — the wallet-api
# repo's `docker compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up --build --wait` stack).
# Absolute https URLs pass through unchanged — the staging backend serves
# wildcard CORS, so it works cross-origin without the proxy. This is the
# value the GitHub Pages branch deploys bake in at build time (see
# .github/workflows/deploy-pages-branch.yml):
#VITE_WALLET_API_URL=https://wallet-api.staging.unicity.network
VITE_WALLET_API_URL=/wallet-api

# Composition assert (#351). Set on deployments that INTEND wallet-api
# custody (the Pages workflow sets it next to VITE_WALLET_API_URL): when
# truthy ('false'/'0' count as unset) and VITE_WALLET_API_URL is missing or
# empty, provider composition throws instead of silently falling back to the
# legacy local-custody bundle — a missing URL would change the custody model,
# not just degrade a feature. Leave unset for intentionally legacy builds.
#VITE_REQUIRE_WALLET_API=true

# LOCAL dev-stack engine override (used by the two-profile smoke): point the
# v2 token engine at the mock aggregator AND the trustbase that same gateway
# serves. Set BOTH or neither — never mix a gateway with another network's
# trustbase. Relative values ride the dev/preview proxy
# (AGGREGATOR_PROXY_TARGET, default http://127.0.0.1:3001).
#VITE_AGGREGATOR_URL=/local-agg
#VITE_TRUSTBASE_URL=/local-agg/trustbase.json

# Sentry error reporting (@sentry/react). The production DSN is baked into the
# bundle (src/config/sentry.ts) — a DSN is not a secret, it can only submit
# events. Dev builds don't report by default: set a DSN here to report from
# `npm run dev`, or set to empty at build time to ship with Sentry disabled.
#VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Welcome DM
VITE_WELCOME_AGENT_NAMETAG=kbbot
VITE_WELCOME_DELAY_MS=4000

# Dev server HTTPS (optional)
SSL_CERT_PATH=
HMR_HOST=

# Deployment base path
BASE_PATH=/

# Subscription gateway (SGW) — per-wallet aggregator subscription keys.
# The SGW is the aggregator gateway, so when VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_API_URL is
# unset the app derives the base from the SDK's per-network config and calls
# it directly (all SGW endpoints serve CORS —
# unicitynetwork/aggregator-subscription#57). Set /sgw (below) to ride the
# dev/preview proxy to a LOCAL SGW stack instead (SGW_PROXY_TARGET, default
# http://127.0.0.1:8080).
#
# LEAVE UNSET unless you are pointing at a LOCAL SGW: the derived value FOLLOWS
# the active network, a pinned one does not. Pinning it to a network's gateway
# means that after a network switch the wallet keeps calling the OLD network's
# SGW; the challenge it returns names that network, the wallet refuses to sign
# it ("network mismatch" — src/services/sgwChallenge.ts), and no subscription
# key can be provisioned on the new network.
#
# The flags compare against EXACTLY 'true'; anything else is off.
# In the Docker image the two flags come from the container env at runtime
# (SUBSCRIPTION_ENABLED / PAID_PLANS_ENABLED) via
# window.__SPHERE_RUNTIME_CONFIG__ — see deploy/runtime-config.sh and
# src/config/subscription.ts. VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_MOCK is dev-only and
# deliberately NOT runtime-swappable.
#VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_API_URL=/sgw
VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_ENABLED=false
VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_MOCK=false
# Paid-plan purchases, one flag per kind of network. Both read EXACTLY 'true'.
#
#              | testnet | mainnet
#   staging    |  sells  |  sells      _TESTNET=true   _MAINNET=true
#   production |  hides  |  sells      _TESTNET unset  _MAINNET=true
#
# Production leaves _TESTNET unset on purpose: a test network's tokens are
# worthless, so charging real money for a key that only works there is the one
# mistake this pair exists to prevent. Staging sets it because rehearsing that
# purchase is what staging is for.
#
# Which network answers to which flag is an allowlist in the app
# (config/networkCapabilities.ts requiresSalesOptIn), not a match on the
# network's name — a future testnet needs no new variable here.
#
# Neither flag is the whole answer: a purchase surface also needs the network's
# gateway to actually price a plan, so an unpriced gateway sells nothing
# whatever these say.
#VITE_PAID_PLANS_ENABLED_TESTNET=false
#VITE_PAID_PLANS_ENABLED_MAINNET=false
#
# Legacy, deployment-wide. Still honoured for MAINNET when _MAINNET is unset, so
# a build can ship before the env is renamed. Never covers test networks.
#VITE_PAID_PLANS_ENABLED=false


# --- NETWORKS / MAINNET ----------------------------------------------------
# The wallet offers a network only when ALL of these hold:
#   (a) the SDK knows it          — a canonical networkId in its NETWORKS table
#   (b) THIS deployment serves it — a wallet-api URL exists for it (below)
#   (c) real-value networks only: VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_ENABLED=true — mainnet
#       refuses the shared build-time aggregator key, which ships readable to
#       every visitor, so provider composition would throw without it
#   (d) mainnet only: the rollout switch is on
# (a) IS NOW TRUE. The bump to sphere-sdk 0.16.0 gave NETWORKS.mainnet a
# networkId, an embedded mainnet trust base, the live gateway and its own token
# registry — the one gate this deployment did not control opened by itself, with
# no change in this repo. Mainnet is held here now only by (b) and (c), both of
# which are yours: WALLET_API_URL_MAINNET, VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_ENABLED=true (a
# real-value network refuses the shared build-time aggregator key) and the
# rollout switch. Setting a mainnet URL early is still safe on its own; arming
# MAINNET_ROLLOUT_ENABLED is now the last step, not one of several.
#
# What FOLLOWS the network automatically (never configure per network): the
# aggregator gateway URL (the SGW base is derived from it), Nostr and group
# relays, the token registry, the trust base, networkId. The SDK's NETWORKS
# table carries no IPFS entry — the wallet makes no IPFS calls.
#
# PER-NETWORK wallet-api backends. One URL cannot serve two networks: the SDK
# client is bound to the active network and a backend configured for another
# one refuses its sign-in, killing the whole asset path. Empty/unset for a
# network = this deployment does not offer it (its row stays unselectable).
# In Docker these come from the CONTAINER env of the same name WITHOUT the
# VITE_ prefix (WALLET_API_URL_MAINNET, no rebuild) and ride
# window.__SPHERE_RUNTIME_CONFIG__: they gate a branch, and the sed-placeholder
# mechanism cannot carry those — it would fold to "available" in every image.
# See src/config/runtimeConfig.ts.
#VITE_WALLET_API_URL_TESTNET2=
#VITE_WALLET_API_URL_MAINNET=
#
# Deliberate mainnet go-live switch; EXACTLY 'true' or it stays off. Keeps a
# routine config change from becoming a launch.
#VITE_MAINNET_ROLLOUT_ENABLED=false
#
# The legacy single VITE_WALLET_API_URL above still works and means "the build
# default network's backend" (testnet2) — it can never serve mainnet.
#
# What a mainnet deployment must still supply:
#   VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_ENABLED=true — REQUIRED on mainnet, and the reason is not
#                              convenience. The key below is substituted into the
#                              JS the browser downloads, so a static aggregator
#                              key is NOT a secret on any client — every visitor
#                              can read it from devtools and spend the operator's
#                              quota. With subscriptions on there is no shared key
#                              in the bundle at all: each wallet signs a challenge
#                              for its own SGW key, metered and revocable per key.
#                              The app refuses to start on a real-value network
#                              with subscriptions off.
#   VITE_AGGREGATOR_API_KEY  — LEAVE UNSET on mainnet: it is ignored entirely
#                              when VITE_SUBSCRIPTION_ENABLED=true, and setting
#                              it is only a way to leak a real key if that flag
#                              is ever wrong (it must be EXACTLY 'true').
#   VITE_PAID_PLANS_ENABLED  — 'true' to sell paid plans on mainnet.
# See docs/DEVOPS-MAINNET.md for the full deployment checklist.
